    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on wolfram2002-ch02-13: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.86";
    dc:description "The negative limitation is refuted by numerous directly inspectable program explorations, and novel regularities are reproducible. Whether discoveries are fundamental is evaluative, but the substantive capability claim is resolvable.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/computation";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Run non-equation-defined programs and document novel, reproducible regularities in their outputs that were not obtained by solving traditional equations. Explicit examples confirm that computers support this broader mode of scientific discovery.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Fundamental is a historical value judgment rather than a quantitative property.";
